        "id": 221116,
        "name": "robertmaxfreeman",
        "username": "robertmaxfreeman",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/robertmaxfreeman/{size}/2147_2.png",
        "created_at": "2018-09-28T14:41:01.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"MindWanderer\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mindwanderer/48/4816_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> MindWanderer:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I use F5 Bunker and F5 AZ frequently.&nbsp; Reveal the top card of each deck and pick one to play, or deal a little bit of self-damage to dig through your deck and pull out any Ongoing you want.&nbsp; Sometimes XPW AA–a bit of damage for another hero’s power use and a play is quite nice.A lot depends on whether you have heroes that can trigger another hero’s power, though.&nbsp; If you have Grandpa Legacy, using him on Requital CC is pointless (he has no deck), but using him on F5 Bunker is even better.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I like it! I thought of Bunker, but hadn’t thought of using F5 AZ (my favorite AZ) to search your deck for ongoing cards. All the options above are good.</p>\n<p>Cosmic Inventor Writhe is another great choice, as is Dark Visionary for villain deck control. If you have any sort of damage prevention, Prime Wardens Tempest is also a nice choice, allowing up to 3 extra plays each turn (as long as you can mitigate the damage).</p>",
